    "/api/v1/linkedin/person": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "linkedinPerson",
        "summary": "Look up a LinkedIn person",
        "description": "One person's LinkedIn relationship with each connected account, read live from LinkedIn: connected or not, any pending invite and when it was sent, and the conversation.\n\nRequires the `leads:read` scope.\n\n**Response.** `{ \"person\": { providerId, publicIdentifier, name, headline } | null, \"accounts\": [account, …] }`, one entry per connected LinkedIn account.\n\nAn account read in full is `{ account, connectedAs, state: \"ok\", connected, invite, revnuInvite, messages, messagesTruncated, lastReplyAt }`:\n\n- `connected` is `true` when this account and the person are first-degree connections.\n- `invite` is the request LinkedIn reports between them, or `null`: `{ direction: \"sent\" | \"received\" | null, status: \"pending\" | \"ignored\" | \"withdrawn\", at }`, where `at` is when it was sent (epoch milliseconds) if LinkedIn says.\n- `revnuInvite` is Revnu's own record when Revnu sent the invite from this account: `{ sentAt, acceptedAt, withdrawnAt }`. `acceptedAt` is when Revnu first saw the person connected, not LinkedIn's exact time.\n- `messages` are the newest 50 in the conversation, oldest first: `{ at, from: \"you\" | \"them\", sentBy, kind, text }`. `sentBy` is `\"agent\"` when Revnu sent it, `\"person\"` when someone replied from Revnu's inbox, and `null` when it was typed in LinkedIn. `messagesTruncated` says older messages exist.\n- `lastReplyAt` is the time of their newest message, or `null`.\n\nAn account that could not be read has a `state` instead: `not_connected`, `needs_reauth` (reconnect it in the dashboard), `paced` with `message` and `retryAt` (the account's daily profile-lookup budget is spent), or `error` with `message`, including when no profile matches.\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| 400 | `profile` is missing or is not a LinkedIn profile URL or id. |\n| 404 | No connected LinkedIn account has the name in `account`. |",
        "tags": [
          "API Reference"
        ],
        "externalDocs": {
          "url": "https://revnu.com/docs/linkedin-person"
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "personalToken": []
          }
        ],
        "x-revnu-scope": "leads:read",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "profile",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Required. A linkedin.com/in/ URL, a public id such as tom-park, or a member id (ACoAA…).",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "account",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "The name of one connected LinkedIn account in your workspace. Without it, every connected account is checked.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ \"person\": { providerId, publicIdentifier, name, headline } | null, \"accounts\": [account, …] }, one entry per connected LinkedIn account. An account read in full is { account, connectedAs, state: \"ok\", connected, invite, revnuInvite, messages, messagesTruncated, lastReplyAt }: - connected is true w",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "profile is missing or is not a LinkedIn profile URL or id.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No connected LinkedIn account has the name in account.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/RateLimited"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unavailable"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/setup": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "setupStatus",
        "summary": "Get setup status",
        "description": "Where a new account is in setup (website, researching, review, payment, start or done) and the exact next step. Works before the account has paid.\n\n**Response.** ```json\n{ \"setup\": { \"stage\": \"review\", \"next\": \"Show the customer what Revnu understood…\", \"account\": { \"name\": \"Acme\", \"website\": \"https://acme.com\" }, \"dashboardUrl\": \"https://revnu.com/dashboard\", \"review\": { \"businessName\": \"Acme\", \"researchFailed\": false, \"rows\": [{ \"id\": \"sells\", \"kind\": \"fact\", \"label\": \"What You Sell\", \"found\": \"Invoicing for agencies\", \"sources\": [\"https://acme.com\"], \"required\": true }] } } }\n```\n\n`stage` is one of `website`, `researching`, `review`, `payment`, `start` and `done`. `researching` adds `research` (the current step and findings so far); `review` adds `review.rows`; `payment` adds `payment` (price, trial days). Follow `next`.",
        "tags": [
          "API Reference"
        ],
        "externalDocs": {
          "url": "https://revnu.com/docs/setup-status"
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "personalToken": []
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "``json { \"setup\": { \"stage\": \"review\", \"next\": \"Show the customer what Revnu understood…\", \"account\": { \"name\": \"Acme\", \"website\": \"https://acme.com\" }, \"dashboardUrl\": \"https://revnu.com/dashboard\", \"review\": { \"businessName\": \"Acme\", \"researchFailed\": false, \"rows\": [{ \"id\": \"sells\", \"kind\": \"fact",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "429": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/RateLimited"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unavailable"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/setup/website": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "setupWebsite",
        "summary": "Set the business website",
        "description": "Give a new account its website. Revnu checks the site exists, then researches the business, which takes about a minute.\n\n**Response.** `200 { \"ok\": true }`. Then poll [setup status](/docs/setup-status) until the stage is `review`.\n\nA site that doesn't exist or isn't answering returns `409` with a message to check the address. An account that already has a website returns `409`, unless its research failed, in which case a corrected address starts it again.",
        "tags": [
          "API Reference"
        ],
        "externalDocs": {
          "url": "https://revnu.com/docs/setup-website"
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "personalToken": []
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "200 { \"ok\": true }. Then poll setup status until the stage is review. A site that doesn't exist or isn't answering returns 409 with a message to check the address. An account that already has a website returns 409, unless its research failed, in which case a corrected address starts it again.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "409": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Conflict"
          },
          "429": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/RateLimited"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unavailable"
          }
        }
      }
    },
